<div class="hero">
  <h1>FastAPI Backend</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">REST API &middot; SSE Streaming &middot; Repository Pattern &middot; SQLAlchemy ORM</p>
  <p>The server-side engine powering the AI Hedge Fund web application.</p>
  <p>
    <span class="badge blue">FastAPI</span>
    <span class="badge green">SSE</span>
    <span class="badge yellow">SQLAlchemy</span>
    <span class="badge red">Alembic</span>
  </p>
</div>

<div class="intro-box">
  <h3>🍽️ The Restaurant Analogy</h3>
  <p>Think of this FastAPI backend as a <strong>restaurant's kitchen</strong>. The React frontend is the <strong>dining room</strong> where customers (users) place orders (analysis requests). The API routes are the <strong>waiters</strong> — they take orders from the dining room and carry them into the kitchen. The services (<code>AgentService</code>, <code>BacktestService</code>, <code>GraphService</code>) are the <strong>chefs</strong> — they do the real cooking (orchestrating agents, compiling graphs, running backtests). The repositories are the <strong>pantry managers</strong> — they know exactly where every ingredient (data record) is stored and how to retrieve it. And the SQLite database is the <strong>pantry</strong> itself — the physical storage where all ingredients and recipes are kept.</p>
  <p>SSE streaming? That's the <strong>kitchen window</strong> where chefs slide finished plates out — the dining room can see dishes being completed one by one, rather than waiting for the entire multi-course meal to be ready.</p>
</div>

<nav class="toc" id="toc"></nav>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<h2 id="architecture">Architecture Overview</h2>

<p>The backend follows a strict layered architecture: routes handle HTTP concerns, services contain business logic, and repositories manage data access. SSE streaming is an orthogonal concern that cuts across the service and route layers.</p>

<div class="diagram-container" aria-label="Backend architecture diagram">
<pre class="mermaid">
flowchart TB
    subgraph Routes["API Routes Layer"]
        HFRoute["hedge_fund.py\n/api/hedge-fund/run\n/api/hedge-fund/backtest"]
        FlowRoute["flows.py\n/api/flows CRUD"]
        RunRoute["flow_runs.py\n/api/flow-runs"]
        KeyRoute["api_keys.py\n/api/api-keys"]
        ModelRoute["models.py\n/api/language-models"]
        OllamaRoute["ollama.py\n/api/ollama/*"]
    end

    subgraph Services["Service Layer"]
        AgentSvc["AgentService\nOrchestrates run_hedge_fund\nEmits SSE events"]
        BTSvc["BacktestService\nHistorical replay engine"]
        GraphSvc["GraphService\nDAG validation\nTopological sort\nConfig resolution"]
    end

    subgraph Repos["Repository Layer"]
        FlowRepo["FlowRepository\nHedgeFundFlow CRUD"]
        RunRepo["RunRepository\nFlowRun + Cycle persistence"]
        KeyRepo["KeyRepository\nApiKey encryption/storage"]
    end

    subgraph DB["Database"]
        SQLite[("SQLite\nWAL mode\nAlembic migrations")]
    end

    subgraph Streaming["SSE Stream"]
        Events["BaseEvent\nStartEvent\nProgressUpdateEvent\nErrorEvent\nCompleteEvent"]
        ESR["EventSourceResponse"]
    end

    HFRoute --> AgentSvc
    HFRoute --> BTSvc
    FlowRoute --> GraphSvc
    RunRoute --> RunRepo
    KeyRoute --> KeyRepo
    ModelRoute --> AgentSvc

    AgentSvc -->|"yields"| Events
    Events --> ESR
    ESR -.->|"SSE stream"| HFRoute

    AgentSvc --> FlowRepo
    BTSvc --> RunRepo
    GraphSvc --> FlowRepo

    FlowRepo --> SQLite
    RunRepo --> SQLite
    KeyRepo --> SQLite
</pre>
</div>

