<!-- ============================================================ -->
<h2 id="edge-cases">Edge Cases &amp; Error Handling</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Behavior</th><th>Error Code</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>SSE connection drops mid-run</strong></td>
      <td>The agent pipeline continues executing server-side. Results are persisted to the database regardless. The client can reconnect and poll <code>/api/flow-runs/{id}</code> for final results. <code>EventSource</code> auto-reconnects with <code>Last-Event-ID</code>.</td>
      <td>N/A (client-side)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>SQLite database lock</strong></td>
      <td>With WAL mode enabled, readers never block writers and vice versa. A busy timeout of 5 seconds handles brief contention. If the timeout expires, the operation retries once before returning a 503.</td>
      <td>503</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Invalid graph config (cycles)</strong></td>
      <td>The <code>GraphService.validate_dag()</code> method detects cycles via DFS coloring. Returns a 422 with a message identifying the nodes involved in the cycle.</td>
      <td>422</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Missing or expired API key</strong></td>
      <td>When an agent attempts to call an LLM provider without a valid key, the service catches the auth error, emits an <code>ErrorEvent</code>, and marks the run as <code>failed</code> with a descriptive message.</td>
      <td>SSE ErrorEvent</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Flow not found</strong></td>
      <td>Requesting a run with a non-existent <code>flow_id</code> returns a 404 before any execution begins.</td>
      <td>404</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Ollama not running</strong></td>
      <td>Proxy endpoints to <code>/api/ollama/*</code> return a 502 with a message indicating the local Ollama service is unreachable.</td>
      <td>502</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

